		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5072&amp;p=36848#p36848"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I have a TYT MD-UV390 radio. I'm running the openGD77 firmware. Something weird is happening when I try to transmit to a Retevis RT-97P DMR repeater. When I transmit, the repeater doesn't see the transmission and it's not repeated. The repeater is in the same room as me.<br><br>However, if I transmit with a different radio, a Retevis RT29d, the repeater sees that. The screen on the repeater screen shows R-T slot 1 when receiving (and repeating) the transmission. And I receive the transmission on the md-UV390. For a few seconds after that, if I transmit with the MD-UV390, it works. But after a few seconds, the repeater no longer displays "R-T slot 1" and at that point I cannot transmit from the MD-UV390.<br><br>So clearly the radio is capable of transmitting to the repeater, but it only works for a short time after another radio transmits to it, and it hasn't closed out that session.<br><br>I have tried opengd77 stable version 20240908 as well as beta version 20250323. <br><br>I have programmed in my channel with the CPS, as well as directly to the radio in VFO mode and it acts the same.<br><br>Channel settings in the TYT with OpenGD77:<br>Rx: 451.800<br>Tx: 456.800<br>Mode: DMR<br>Location: No<br>DMR ID: none (despite programming one with the CPS. If I enter a dummy number here like 12345 it doesn't change anything)<br>Color code: 5<br>Timeslot: 1<br>TG Lst: RxSite (the correct talkgroup)<br>Contact: None<br>Rx/Tx CSS: N/A<br>Step: 2.5 khz<br>Vox: Off<br>Ch Power: Master (5 w)<br>Eco: Yes<br>TS Tx Ts1:off<br>TS Tx TS2:off<br>APRS: None<br>For DMO: No<br><br>Quick settings:<br>Filter: None<br>DMR Filter: None<br>CC Scan: On<br>TS Filter: Off<br>Talkaround: Off<br>Roaming: Off<br>Mute: No<br><br>Repeater settings:<br>Rx Freq: 456.800<br>Tx Freq: 451.800<br>Decode/Encode (greyed out, presumably only for analog): 136.5<br>Rx Color: 5<br>Tx Color: 5<br>Band (greyed out): W<br>Power: High<br>Ana/Dig: DMR</div></blockquote>Hello, i have same problem with my MD-9600 and MMDVM dual hat hotspot. Radio is able to hit my hotspot 1 time on 100 but, if there is some qso into the other slot, radio hits the hotspot without problems.<br>No problem with some other radios.<br>Another quirks is that on several repeaters near me, BER is always 2,5% or more<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=558">IK1HJT</a> — Sat Apr 19, 2025 5:23 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
